A||N||7||Sage||headlights...again||||5||
Z||000000||Sage||04-07-2000||12:45 PM||||     I know the headlight situation has been covered, and covered, and covered, but I have not seen this problem yet.  <P>     car:86GT<BR>     Problem: When the headlight switch is pushed, the lights come on but the motors do not activate.  If the switch is held in a position between on and off, the motors activate, and the lights come up normally.  When the switch is turned off, everything works as it should. At first I thought,"simple, bad switch", put known good switch from another car in and it does the same thing.  Haven't tried replacing it yet, but would the main relay,(the one on the drivers side inner fender), being bad cause this situation?  Just thought I would see if anybody else has seen/dealt with this problem before.<P>    TIA for any ideas, suggestions, solutions.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||04-07-2000||08:42 PM||||I can't think of anything other than the switch that would do this. You may have damaged the second switch taking it out. They aren't the most rugged headlight switch I've ever seen.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sage||04-07-2000||10:43 PM||||Thanks Ogre,  I thought the same thing, so put the original "bad" switch in the second car and it operates normally!  Put the switch removed from the second car back in its original spot and everything is as it should be.  Got me stumped.  I will try switching out the relay, but I don't see how it can make any difference!  Just seems that the switch is the only thing that could cause this situation.  Will keep looking, if you come up with any ideas, would appreciate any and all input.  Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000003||fieroshop||04-07-2000||11:20 PM||||I've had that problem come up severl times and everytime I had to replace the light relay. That is the one not next to the light motor. It is the one on the front firewall and depending on the year it could be under the fender.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sage||04-08-2000||12:14 AM||||Thanks George,  that's basicly what I was trying to figure out.  Although I can't understand how it could work that way, the only things I can think of that would cause the symptom would be the switch or the connector that it plugs into.  Just seems that if the switch activates the relay, and it works at all, it should spin the motors.  Having to hold the switch in the half open position, sure does suggest (to me anyway) that the switch is not making good contact inside.  I took these switches apart thinking I could clean, bend, or otherwise alter them to work, but they are pretty straight forward in thier operation, and I got the same results afterward!  All I know is that both switches work just fine in the other car(the one without the problem), but niether will work in the car WITH the problem!  Oh well, live and learn!  Just glad the forum is here as at LEAST a sounding board.  <P>     Again, thanks for the input, and I will be changing the relay to see what happens.<P>               Pax  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000005||Majik||06-29-2000||12:48 AM||||Sorry to bring this back up (I know you all are saying headlights?  again?)  but I'm having the same problem...except I can't get the half-way trick to work. <P>problem: both headlights won't go up, but go down fine...happened at the same time (so it really can't be headlight specific...changed the switch..nothing.<P>Did replacing that part do the trick for you?  I'm getting one tomorrow...just curious.  again, sorry for bringing it back up||||reg||5
Z||000006||SeanyD||06-29-2000||01:42 AM||||my headlighsts seem to do the exact opposite.  the go up fine...but to make them go down or even off you have to turn the switch off, then to parking lights only, then off!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||06-29-2000||09:25 AM||||SeanyD--Try pushing the switch gently to either the left or right when you turn them off.  That's what I have to do once in a while.||||reg||1
